From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: intel: chtwc_int33fe: GPD Win: request 5 V only from USB-PD chargers

The GPD Win is specified for a 5 V / 2.5 A charger, but the sink PDOs also
offer 5-12 V, so a USB-PD charger supplies 9 or 12 V. Sink one fixed 5 V PDO
at up to 2.5 A instead. (Local patch: the GPD Pocket shares the DMI match and
ships with a 12 V charger.)
---
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/chtwc_int33fe.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/chtwc_int33fe.c
@@ -98,9 +98,13 @@
 	PDO_FIXED(5000, 1500, PDO_FIXED_FLAGS),
 };
 
+/*
+ * GPD Win: sink at 5 V only, up to 2.5 A (GPD's specification for this device: a 5 V / 2.5 A charger).
+ * Upstream also offers 5-12 V, so USB-PD chargers ran it at 9 or 12 V. The GPD Pocket, which shares
+ * this driver and DMI match, ships with a 12 V charger, so this stays a local GPD Win patch.
+ */
 static const u32 snk_pdo[] = {
-	PDO_FIXED(5000, 400, PDO_FIXED_FLAGS),
-	PDO_VAR(5000, 12000, 3000),
+	PDO_FIXED(5000, 2500, PDO_FIXED_FLAGS),
 };
 
 static const struct software_node pi3usb30532_node = {
